a) In general, we can show that  $n^2$  divides  $(n-1)(n+1)^{n+1}+1$  for  $n>1.$  We have
\begin{align*}(n-1)(n+1)^{n+1}+1 &= (n^2-1)(n+1)^n+1 
&\equiv -(n+1)^n+1\pmod{n^2} 
&= -\left(1+\binom{n}{1}\cdot n+\binom{n}{2}\cdot n^2+\dots\right)+1 
&\equiv -(1+n^2)+1\equiv 0\pmod{n^2}.\end{align*}
Putting  $n=2010$  gives the particular case  $4040100\mid 2009\cdot2011^{2011}+1.$

